.Dt MBT_BE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_be_value_parse ,
.Nm mbt_be_value_encode ,
.Nm mbt_be_value_free ,
.Nm mbt_be_value_freep ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append_number ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append_string ,
.Nm mbt_be_list_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_list_append ,
.Nm mbt_be_string_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_find ,
.Nm mbt_be_walk ,
.Nm mbt_be_pp
.Nd Bencode parsing and construction library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/be.h
.Fn mbt_be_value_parse "const unsigned char *buf" "size_t sz" "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_value_encode "struct mbt_be_value *v" "unsigned char **out" "size_t *len"
.Fn mbt_be_value_free "struct mbt_be_value *v"
.Fn mbt_be_value_freep "struct mbt_be_value **v"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_new "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "struct mbt_be_value *value"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append_number "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "int64_t num"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append_string "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "const void *buf" "size_t len"
.Fn mbt_be_list_new "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_list_append "struct mbt_be_value *list" "struct mbt_be_value *val"
.Fn mbt_be_string_new "struct mbt_be_value **out" "const void *buf" "size_t len"
.Fn mbt_be_find "struct mbt_be_value *be" "const char *key"
.Fn mbt_be_walk "struct mbt_be_value *be" "int (*cb)(struct mbt_be_value *, void *)" "void *arg"
.Fn mbt_be_pp "struct mbt_be_value *be" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_be
library provides utilities for parsing, constructing, and traversing
bencoded data structures. Bencoding is the serialization format used by
the BitTorrent protocol.
.Pp
All operations revolve around the
.Vt mbt_be_value
structure, which can represent a string, an integer, a list, or a
dictionary.
.Sh PARSING AND ENCODING
.Fn mbt_be_value_parse
takes a buffer of bencoded bytes and produces a tree of
.Vt mbt_be_value
structures.
.Fn mbt_be_value_encode
encodes a tree of
.Vt mbt_be_value
structures back into a dynamically allocated buffer of bencoded bytes.
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned buffer.
.Pp
The following functions handle memory management:
.Fn mbt_be_value_free
destroys a single
.Vt mbt_be_value
node and its children.
.Fn mbt_be_value_freep
is a convenience wrapper for freeing a pointer to a
.Vt mbt_be_value.
.Sh CONSTRUCTION
To create bencoded data, use the following factory functions:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_new
Creates a new empty dictionary.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_list_new
Creates a new empty list.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_string_new
Creates a new string value from an existing buffer of bytes.
.El
.Pp
Once structures are created, they can be populated:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_append
Appends a previously created
.Vt mbt_be_value
to a dictionary using the provided key.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_append_number
Appends an integer value to a dictionary with the given key.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It Fn mbt_be_dict_append_string
Appends raw bytes as a string to a dictionary with the given key.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_list_append
Adds a value to the end of the specified list.
.El
.Sh TRAVERSAL AND INSPECTION
.Fn mbt_be_find
searches for a key within a dictionary and returns the associated
.Vt mbt_be_value. Returns
.Fa NULL
if the key is not found.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_be_walk
performs a depth-first traversal of the bencoded structure, invoking a
callback function for every node encountered.
.Pp
The following functions are for debugging or utility:
.Fn mbt_be_pp
pretty-prints the bencoded structure (e.g., to a file or stdout via an argument).
.Fn mbt_be_streq
(inline) checks if a bencoded string node contains the exact bytes of a
provided C string.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Most functions return 0 on success or a negative error code on failure.
Construction and parsing functions that allocate memory return
.Fa NULL
on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Constructing a simple dictionary:
.Bd -literal
struct mbt_be_value *dict;
mbt_be_dict_new(&dict);

mbt_be_dict_append_number(dict, "length", 1024);
mbt_be_dict_append_string(dict, "name", "my_torrent", 9);

// 'dict' now contains a bencoded dictionary: i1024e#name#my_torrent
.Ed
